+## [06/05/2026 23:59] - US-012
+- What was implemented: Mode transitions with animated crossfade/slide, animated entry for album art and text on track change, WebSocket reconnection with exponential backoff, and screen-wake reconnection via lifecycle observer
+- Files changed: android/app/build.gradle.kts, android/app/src/main/java/com/mediacontrol/app/MainActivity.kt, android/app/src/main/java/com/mediacontrol/app/websocket/WebSocketClient.kt, android/app/src/main/java/com/mediacontrol/app/viewmodel/PlaybackViewModel.kt, android/app/src/main/java/com/mediacontrol/app/ui/PlayerScreen.kt, android/app/src/main/java/com/mediacontrol/app/ui/LyricsScreen.kt, android/AGENTS.md, prd.json, progress.txt
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Patterns discovered: Use `AnimatedContent` with `slideInHorizontally` + `fadeIn` togetherWith `slideOutHorizontally` + `fadeOut` for mode transitions in `MediaControlApp`
+  - Patterns discovered: Use `AnimatedContent` with `fadeIn() togetherWith fadeOut()` for track change animations on album art and metadata; wrap `AsyncImage` in a `Box` to hold `weight` modifier outside `AnimatedContent`
+  - Patterns discovered: WebSocket auto-reconnection implemented directly in `WebSocketClient` with exponential backoff (1s base, 30s cap, shift up to 5); use `CoroutineScope` for scheduling retries
+  - Patterns discovered: Screen-wake reconnection via `DisposableEffect` + `LocalLifecycleOwner.current` in `MainActivity`, observing `Lifecycle.Event.ON_START`
+  - Gotchas encountered: `viewModelScope` from `lifecycle-viewmodel-ktx:2.7.0` was not resolving despite adding the dependency — used a custom `CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.Main)` instead
+  - Gotchas encountered: `AnimatedContent` wraps content in a `Box` internally, so `weight` modifiers don't work inside it — wrap the `AnimatedContent` in a parent `Box` with the weight modifier
+  - Useful context: `onScreenWake()` in ViewModel checks if state is `Disconnected` or `Error` before reconnecting to avoid duplicate connections
+  - Useful context: `DisposableEffect` properly cleans up the lifecycle observer via `onDispose` to prevent leaks
+---

